#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Polished demo videos of Search, recorded from a script, nobody's screen taken.

    ./demo record SCRIPT.json OUT.mp4 [--keep] [--prores] [--4k]
                                  launch Search in a demo world of its own, seeded from the
                                  script; record only its window (ScreenCaptureKit, 60 fps,
                                  2×) while the steps run through the bench; then compose:
                                  background, shadow, rounded corners, a drawn pointer and
                                  camera moves → OUT.mp4 (libx264 -crf 16, yuv420p), and
                                  OUT.mov in ProRes 422 HQ with --prores. --keep leaves the
                                  raw recording and plan in OUT.mp4.work/ for `compose`.
    ./demo compose WORK OUT.mp4   compose again from a kept OUT.mp4.work/ (no app needed)
    ./demo check SCRIPT.json      read the script and say what it would do; starts nothing
    ./demo fake OUT.mp4 [--prores] [--4k]
                                  the composer on a made-up recording (ffmpeg's test
                                  pattern): checks background, shadow, pointer and encoding
                                  without Search or Screen Recording
    ./demo selftest               what ScreenCaptureKit gives for a window of the helper's own
                                  placed off every screen (needs Screen Recording)
    ./demo build                  build the Swift helper, build/demo-capture

Search must be built first (./build.sh → build/Search.app). The window is
ordered in far off every screen (bench `stage`), so it shows on no display,
and the app is never made active; only that window is recorded, without the
real pointer. The demo world is wiped afterwards, as Tests/split_view.py's
finish() does. Screen Recording must be allowed for the app that runs this
(Terminal, or Claude): macOS names it in System Settings › Privacy & Security
› Screen & System Audio Recording. Nothing here asks for it.

THE SCRIPT (JSON; YAML if PyYAML is installed) — Tests/demo/example.json is a
~30 s showcase. Every key is optional:

  window      {"width": 1440, "height": 900}            the browser window, in points
  output      {"width": 1920, "height": 1080, "fps": 60, "crf": 16, "prores": false,
               "margin": 0.07, "radius": 16, "cursor": 1}   (3840×2160 for 4K; cursor 0: none)
  background  {"image": PATH, "blur": 0}               default: a soft blurred gradient
  look        "light" | "dark" | "system"
  settings    {"sidebar": true, "layout.cards": true, "spaces": true, "splitView": true, …}
              raw defaults keys of the demo world's own suite, written before launch
  spaces      [{"name", "colour": "blue"|0…5, "tabs": [{"name", "url", "group"}],
                "pins": [{"url", "listed"}], "folders": [{"name", "pins": [URL…], "folded"}]}]
              URLs are https://…, or local:NAME for a page the harness serves
  start       {"space": 1, "tab": NAME}
  lead, tail  seconds at rest before the first step and after the last; settle: before recording
  steps       [{"do": ACTION, "at": SECONDS | "wait": SECONDS, …}]  ("at" from the first step's
              start; "wait" after the step before)

Points ("to", "from") are window points from its top left, "x%,y%" of the window,
"center", or "page:CSS SELECTOR" on the page in front. "@NAME" in a raw bench
request is that tab's id. Actions:

  move   {to, dur=.6, hover}     the drawn pointer glides (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1); hover: the
                                 page hears it pass (bench `pointer`)
  hover  {to, dur}               move with hover
  click  {to?, via="view"|"app"|"page"|"none", then?}   press drawn; the real click through
                                 bench (`split mouse`, `pointer press`), never the Mac's mouse
  tap    {selector, tab?, mods?} pointer to an element, then bench `tap` (a trusted click)
  drag   {from, to, dur=.9}      a drag, drawn and delivered a frame apart
  cursor {visible, jump}
  key    {key: "cmd+shift+h", letgo?}   release {}: the held modifiers let go (⌃Tab)
  type   {text, every=.08}       into what has the keyboard (pointer hidden while typing)
  field  {text}                  the address field's own way
  suggest {pick: "Capture"}      the address field's row whose words hold that, taken
  space  {swipe: -320, ms} | {go: N} | {new: NAME} | {colour}
  split  {pair: [DRAGGED, TARGET], side} | {request: {...}}
  select {tab}    peek {link: SELECTOR | url | close}    pinch {amount=.6, ms=600}
  menu   {title: "Edit Site Style…", menu?}    style {css?, close?}
  zoom   {rect: [x, y, w, h] in window points | "reset", dur=.9}   the camera, in post
  scroll {dy, dx, ms, tab?}   eval {js, tab?}   bench {request: {...}}   wait {}
"""

import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
